[{:seon.task/name "the-process-store-is-made-before-any-shard"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-23 by the walk session: forked-agent tests went red at random under load (seon.repl-test red on 3 agent-process tests, on another run a different one, green alone); one red was :root-did-not-listen, \"Database does not exist\" at target/runs/test-store. Cause, reproduced by the worktree session store at n = 4 shards on a tree without that store: every process test's root opened the one store target/runs/test-store with seon.db/open!, which creates and seeds a store whose data file is missing. Four shards' first roots started at once; one created it, and a root in another shard saw its data file and opened a database not yet made. The first test of shards 2 and 3 went red (seon.agent-test/a-wide-reach-reuses-unchanged-results, an-agent-holds-mains-tests-and-runs-them), and green on a rerun once the store existed. AGENTS section 5 (one store, many branches): the store is made once, before any shard. bin/test seeds it (seon seed 0, as bin/check seeds its store) after building the binary; seon.test-store/process-store names it for root_test and agent_test and refuses, naming bin/test, when it is not made, never creating it. After: the same two namespaces from a fresh tree, all four shards green."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.test-store-test/the-process-store-is-made-before-any-shard}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-test-root-is-its-own"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-23 by root: seon.root-test/main-follows-its-source-tree-across-restarts went red under parallel load (4 of 4 on walk's api branch, once on jolt/an-edge-asks-one-way) and green alone. Its first root's fresh main already held the whole Seon program (:removed-forms 71, file-text answering other files). Cause, found by the worktree session store: root_test's root-answers gave every root on the one test store the runs directory <store>-runs. bin/root start in a runs directory whose root still runs only reports that root's status and port (bin/root's start: running, then status), so seon.test-store/start-root! answered another test's root, one that had imported src. The main itself was cut cleanly from :db, which holds no forms after the agent and root tests. Fixed at both producers: root-answers takes a runs directory per main, and start-root! refuses a runs directory a live root holds (:seon.test-store/runs-in-use), never answering that root."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.test-store-test/a-test-root-is-its-own}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-kept-store-is-keyed-by-its-schema"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-23 by root: the page merge changed three attributes to refs, and every checkout's kept target/program-store and target/runs/test-store refused to open (seon.db/open!: :seon.db/types-differ, another value type than the schema declares). bin/test failed at its plan, and process tests at root start. Both are regenerable output, made again from their inputs, never records. Fix: seon.db/schema-digest names the schema; seon.test-store/kept-store! answers base-<digest> and removes a store at base of another schema (base itself, or base-<8 hex digits>), sparing a runs directory beside it. The test runner's program store and the process store (seon.test-store/process-store, made by the plan's seon.test-store/make-process-store!, which replaces bin/test's seed step) are named by it. A changed schema makes a new store; nothing is migrated or refused."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.test-store-test/a-kept-store-is-keyed-by-its-schema}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-process-root-opens-the-shared-store-under-load"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-25 (jolt/agent-conversation, fa9f597d5): `bin/test seon.agent-test seon.root-test` (two process-test shards, load ~4 on the 18-core machine) went red once on `seon.agent-test/a-blocked-agent-ends-on-its-socket-eof`: `seon.test-store/start-root!` answered a root with :port nil (it died before ROOT LISTENING), so `seon.test-store/ask` failed its contract on :port. Green alone. The dead root's log (target/runs/root-ended-bb0e02e9-1e23-49dd-b3d5-a06c533f2f1e-runs/root.log) says why: `lmdb env_open: Invalid argument` (rc 22, :lmdb-error), raised in `seon.db/open-main!` via datahike.connector/-connect-impl* while opening the one shared process store (`seon.test-store/process-store`, target/runs/test-store-<digest>) that other shards' roots held open. EINVAL from mdb_env_open is what LMDB answers for an environment opened with flags or a map size that disagree with how another process already has it open (the lock file's), or a second open of one env path in a process; which one this is is the task's first measurement. Reproduce: run the two namespaces together at n = 4 shards (bin/test --plan then the shards at once) until a root dies with env_open; read every concurrent root's open flags and map size (`seon.db/store-cfg`). Correct: every process root opens the shared store with the same flags and map size whatever the load, or a refused open is the root's typed error naming the store and the flags that disagree (docs/failure-points.md). A start that dies is the test's error, never a nil port read later. Proof: a deftest that starts n = 4 roots on the process store at once and asserts every one listens."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.test-store-test/n-roots-open-the-process-store-at-once}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-shard-says-what-each-test-waits-on"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the stability sweep of 2026-10-25 (notes/stability-2026-10-25.md; the owner: platform stability first). test side of the sweep (target/waits-test.md in the stability worktree): bin/test waits on its shards in index order (bin/test's wait $P[i]), so a hung shard 1 hides later shards' output; and test waits with no end beyond their answer: ts/ask's socket read of a live parked root (test/seon/test_store.clj:202), start-root!'s wait for ROOT LISTENING (167), stop-root! (207), kill-root! (178), binary-sh of a mode that parks (113), agent_test's and e2e's <!! event loops on an events tap (agent_test.clj:51,82,133,176,349,365,388; e2e.clj:81,236) that skip a dead agent's event, check.clj's await-event with no terminal event named (204,496,510,517,745,980,1156), bare @p / <!! after a synchronous step in procs_test (282-372), problems_test:176, step_test:11-20 (use the answer helper, procs_test.clj:466, or realized?). Correct: bin/test reports each shard as it ends (wait -n), and each test wait names its end: an agent's or root's death event ends an event loop (a loop that skips a death is red), a synchronous step's answer is read with realized? (no wait). The parked-everywhere case is jolt.async/a-process-whose-every-thread-parks-ends-its-waits. Clocks in test (check.clj:879,984,1001,649,1473,67,1135; lib_test.clj:50,81,84) are listed in target/waits-test.md for docs/clocks.md's owner to name or remove."
  :seon.task/kind :work}
 {:seon.task/name "an-agent-test-shares-its-shards-root"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-27: prioritize what speeds up development. Root's analysis (tests-fast, 2026-10-27): 91 process tests are 1,940 s, 83% of suite time; the 55 seon.agent-test/in-agent tests each booted a built root (bin/root start) and dropped its main with a second ./seon process. Measured on a running root: boot 9.5 s of a 15 s test (the source import 4.8 s), attach 0.36 s (66 ms on a warm root), stop 1.3 s, drop about 1 s. Done: seon.test-store/shared-root! starts one root per shard process and root arguments on a main of its own of the process store, stopped and its main dropped at the process's end; in-agent takes forms as a function of the test's names {:ns :task :run :agent} (a fresh task namespace per test, the agent the attach answered), kills its agent and deletes its task's branches at its end; :own-root? keeps a root of its own for a test whose agent merges into main. Replaces the boot, stop and drop process per in-agent test (in-agent's drop-main! call). Not done, and why: the brief's narrower digest (a leaf change reaching no agent test that does not name it) is not honest: seon.root/start! reaches 1,252 of 1,908 src forms and reads the tree (seon.fx/read-source imports it), and the forms an agent evaluates are strings, so an agent test's input stays the tree (binary-sh a tree reader). Follow-up: a scripted model per task (:seon.task/config) would let the :sets tests, one script each, share their shard's root too."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.test-store-test/agent-tests-in-one-process-share-its-root}}]
